Keyword-shaped lines inside a top-level multi-line string or comment are
literal text: no blank line is inserted between an `:ENDIF;` line and an
`:IF` line inside them, and blank lines inside them are not touched
(fmt.blank_line_between_blocks and fmt.max_consecutive_blank_lines, D7).
Kept at top level: inside a procedure, range formatting re-indents the
literal's interior lines, an invariant failure reported separately.
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE sTxt;
sTxt := "header
:ENDIF;
:IF x


footer";
/*
:ENDWHILE
:WHILE y



;
:IF .T.;
sTxt := "";
:ENDIF;
-- format --
